#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Draw parts from their own code, for parts whose library has no page of their own to photograph.

Shaan, 10 Oct: "get maybe all of these components downloaded ... so they can be viewed on the thing". After bin/shoot,
~21,000 parts still had no picture: their sites show them inside one app (catalogs, atomloader) or a gallery per kind
(shadcnui-blocks). Their code is held here, so each is drawn as an app would draw it: its files in a sandbox with React,
shadcn/ui (new-york-v4) and the packages parts use, bundled by esbuild (bin/render-bundle.mjs), styled by Tailwind v4 in
the dark theme, opened headless and photographed like bin/shoot's pictures (thumbs/<registry>/<key>.webp).

  bin/render setup DIR                       # the sandbox: packages, shadcn/ui from ui.shadcn.com, next/* shims, theme
  bin/render --print-jsonl > todo.jsonl      # parts with code and no picture, each with its files (sounds, libs left out)
  UI_THUMBS=<dir> bin/render run DIR < todo.jsonl   # draw them; _rendered.jsonl and _render_failed.jsonl say how it went

A part fails when its bundle needs a package the sandbox lacks (the run ends with the commonest, to install), when it
throws, or when it draws nothing (no elements, or one flat colour). Resumable: a part with a picture is skipped.
"""
